videos.script:
Until now the planner has been a web app in a frame. Today it becomes something else: an app whose screen the phone draws itself. {{native}}

React Native runs your JavaScript and asks the platform for its own controls. {{layers}} A Text becomes a native label. A Pressable becomes a native view that takes touches. There is no HTML, and no CSS.

First, React, in five minutes. {{react}} Components, props and state, enough to write the planner's screen whatever framework you know.

Then a new project, with Expo. {{expo}} And one file that comes across unchanged, byte for byte: the planner's rules. {{rules}} The views do not come across. They are written again, and that is the price of this path.

You will run it in a browser, check the week's total against lesson 4, and weigh what the native views buy against what they cost. {{weigh}}
